---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy - Data Protection & GDPR Compliance"
  description="How newskrypt collects, safeguards, and respects user personal data in compliance with GDPR, CCPA, and global privacy standards."
  canonicalUrl="https://crypto-news-rose.vercel.app/privacy-policy"
>
  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-12 md:py-20">
    <header class="mb-10 pb-6 border-b border-slate-200">
      <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-3 py-1 bg-amber-500/10 border border-amber-500/30 rounded-full text-xs font-extrabold text-amber-800 uppercase tracking-wider mb-4">
        <span>🔒 User Privacy & Data Protection</span>
      </div>
      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl lg:text-5xl font-black text-black tracking-tight mb-3">
        Privacy Policy & Data Rights Statement
      </h1>
      <p class="text-xs text-slate-600 font-medium">Last Reviewed & Formally Ratified: September 2026 | newskrypt Legal & Data Protection Office</p>
    </header>

    <div class="space-y-8 text-sm text-black leading-relaxed">
      <!-- Section 1: Data Minimization & Core Commitment -->
      <section class="bg-white border border-slate-200 p-6 sm:p-8 rounded-2xl shadow-xs">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-black text-black mb-3 flex items-center gap-2">
          <span>1. Data Minimization & Privacy-First Architecture</span>
        </h2>
        <p class="text-black mb-3">
          <strong>newskrypt</strong> champions absolute user privacy and data minimization. We do not sell, rent, barter, or trade personal user information to third-party data brokers, marketing agencies, or corporate entities. Our platform is engineered from the ground up to operate with minimal data collection strictly necessary to deliver real-time news, financial analytics, and interactive market charts securely to your browser.
        </p>
        <p class="text-black">
          Whether you visit <strong>newskrypt</strong> from Europe, North America, Asia-Pacific, or any global jurisdiction, your digital footprint is protected under rigorous encryption standards and data minimization protocols.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 2: Information We Collect -->
      <section class="bg-white border border-slate-200 p-6 sm:p-8 rounded-2xl shadow-xs">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-black text-black mb-3">2. Categories of Information Collected</h2>
        <p class="text-black mb-4">
          To maintain infrastructure performance, prevent denial-of-service (DDoS) attacks, and deliver opt-in news updates, <strong>newskrypt</strong> processes limited data categories:
        </p>

        <div class="space-y-4">
          <div class="p-4 bg-slate-50 border border-slate-200 rounded-xl">
            <h3 class="font-bold text-black text-base mb-1">A. Voluntarily Provided Data</h3>
            <p class="text-slate-800 text-xs sm:text-sm">
              If you subscribe to the <em>newskrypt Daily Dispatch</em> newsletter, submit an news tip, or contact our editorial desk, we store your email address and message contents strictly to fulfill your request. You can opt out or unsubscribe at any time via the one-click link at the bottom of any email dispatch.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div class="p-4 bg-slate-50 border border-slate-200 rounded-xl">
            <h3 class="font-bold text-black text-base mb-1">B. Automated Technical Telemetry</h3>
            <p class="text-slate-800 text-xs sm:text-sm">
              When loading <strong>newskrypt</strong>, our edge servers automatically log anonymized server metrics—including your IP address, browser type, device operating system, referrer URL, and request timestamps. This telemetry is aggregated exclusively for firewall protection, caching speed, and system diagnostic health.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 3: Alignment with Editorial & Publishing Standards -->
      <section class="bg-white border border-slate-200 p-6 sm:p-8 rounded-2xl shadow-xs">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-black text-black mb-3">3. Integration with Editorial & Content Quality Rules</h2>
        <p class="text-black mb-3">
          Our privacy practices directly support the core publishing rules of <strong>newskrypt</strong>:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 text-black">
          <li><strong>No Intrusive Behavioral Tracking:</strong> We do not deploy aggressive cross-site trackers or identity resolution cookies that profile users across external websites.</li>
          <li><strong>Verified Media Integrity:</strong> All images, charts, and technical media hosted on <strong>newskrypt</strong> are served from secure, optimized Content Delivery Networks (CDNs) with zero third-party data extraction. Every article maintains non-duplicate, unique hero images with exact descriptive metadata as governed by our <a href="/editorial-policy" class="text-amber-600 font-bold hover:underline">Editorial Policy</a>.</li>
          <li><strong>Exact Structural Meta Quality:</strong> MetaTitles and MetaDescriptions across all pages strictly follow our 55-character title and 155-character metaDescription publishing constraints, ensuring transparent search previews without deceptive clickbait.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 4: GDPR, CCPA & Global User Rights -->
      <section class="bg-white border border-slate-200 p-6 sm:p-8 rounded-2xl shadow-xs">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-black text-black mb-3">4. GDPR, CCPA & Global Rights Compliance</h2>
        <p class="text-black mb-3">
          Under the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR), California Consumer Privacy Act (CCPA/CPRA), and related international privacy legislation, <strong>newskrypt</strong> guarantees all users the following enforceable rights:
        </p>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-5 space-y-2 text-black">
          <li><strong>Right to Access & Data Portability:</strong> Request a full copy of any personal data linked to your email address in our systems.</li>
          <li><strong>Right to Erasure ("Right to be Forgotten"):</strong> Demand the permanent deletion of your email address, subscription history, or contact logs.</li>
          <li><strong>Right to Restrict or Object to Processing:</strong> Opt out of statistical analytics or communications at any time.</li>
        </ul>
        <div class="mt-6 p-4 bg-slate-50 border border-slate-200 rounded-xl">
          <p class="text-xs text-slate-800">
            To exercise any of your legal privacy rights, submit a formal request to our Data Protection Officer at:
            <code class="block mt-2 font-mono text-xs font-bold text-amber-700">newskryptowahrung26@gmail.com</code>
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 5: Children's Privacy & YMYL Disclosures -->
      <section class="bg-white border border-slate-200 p-6 sm:p-8 rounded-2xl shadow-xs">
        <h2 class="text-xl font-black text-black mb-3">5. Children's Privacy & YMYL Financial Disclaimer</h2>
        <p class="text-black">
          <strong>newskrypt</strong> is targeted at an adult audience seeking financial news and market intelligence. We do not knowingly collect personal data from children under the age of 18. Furthermore, all news reporting on <strong>newskrypt</strong> is subject to our financial non-advisory disclosures detailed in our <a href="/editorial-policy" class="text-amber-600 font-bold hover:underline">Editorial Policy</a> and <a href="/disclaimer" class="text-amber-600 font-bold hover:underline">Financial Disclaimer</a>.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>